MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The classic binding ships Level 1 under the recovered 512 px ClearBlue, which
reads muddy brown at play angles — the recorded reason the binding was once
deviated away entirely. Rather than force the mud or drop the record,
vendor-sky-clearblue-hd.mjs derives clearblue-hd: the same six faces, 2x
upscaled with an unsharp mask and a mild tone lift, 682 KB for the set at q0.9
(the nightsky q1.0 rule is about pixel-scale chroma detail this set does not
have — measured reasoning in the script). The recovered set stays untouched and
selectable at clearblue; the style RECORD keeps the archive's own binding name
and presentation maps it to the HD set, so adapted pixels never masquerade as
recovered ones.

smoke-media's curated-sky check re-keyed on identity, not source prose: it
counted skies whose source string was exactly 'GraphysX archive', which any
honestly-provenanced derived set breaks. The invariant was always 'every
pre-import id survives unreplaced, and only the imports are new' — the check now
says that and is stronger for it (it also pins the post-import count).

Verified: smoke-archive-levels' binding check expects clearblue-hd on Level 1;
smoke-media green with the identity check.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
